<div class="container">
    <div class="content-box hero">
        <h1>Circle Applications</h1>
        <p>Discover how circles shape our world in science, technology, and everyday life.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Engineering & Technology</h2>
        <div class="info-grid">
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>⚙️ Wheels and Gears</h3>
                <p>The wheel, one of humanity's greatest inventions, uses the circle's property of constant radius for smooth rolling motion. Gears transfer rotational motion efficiently using circular toothed wheels.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🎡 Rotating Machinery</h3>
                <p>Motors, turbines, and engines all use circular motion. The crankshaft in car engines converts linear motion to circular rotation through circular components.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>📡 Satellite Dishes</h3>
                <p>Circular parabolic dishes focus electromagnetic waves to a single point, making satellite communication and radio telescopes possible.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🔌 Electrical Components</h3>
                <p>Coils and inductors use circular windings to generate magnetic fields. Circular waveguides transmit electromagnetic energy efficiently.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🚂 Transportation</h3>
                <p>Train wheels, airplane turbines, ship propellers - circular motion drives modern transportation systems worldwide.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>💿 Data Storage</h3>
                <p>CDs, DVDs, and hard disk platters store data in circular tracks. The circular design allows for continuous, efficient read/write operations.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Architecture & Construction</h2>
        <div class="info-grid">
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🏛️ Domes and Arches</h3>
                <p>Circular arches distribute weight evenly, allowing for strong structures. The Pantheon's dome, built in 126 AD, still stands as a testament to circular engineering.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🏰 Towers and Columns</h3>
                <p>Circular cross-sections provide maximum strength with minimum material. Round towers are more resistant to siege weapons and wind forces.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🎭 Amphitheaters</h3>
                <p>Circular or semi-circular designs provide optimal acoustics and sightlines for all audience members, used since ancient Roman times.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🏗️ Roundabouts</h3>
                <p>Circular traffic intersections improve flow and safety by eliminating perpendicular crossings and reducing conflict points.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Science & Nature</h2>
        <div class="info-grid">
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🔬 Particle Accelerators</h3>
                <p>The Large Hadron Collider uses a circular path to accelerate particles to near light speed, making groundbreaking physics discoveries.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🌍 Planetary Orbits</h3>
                <p>While elliptical, many orbits are nearly circular. The circular model helps us understand gravitational motion and plan space missions.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🌊 Wave Propagation</h3>
                <p>Sound waves, water ripples, and electromagnetic radiation spread in circular or spherical patterns from their source.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🧬 Cell Biology</h3>
                <p>Many cells and organelles are spherical or circular in cross-section, optimizing surface area to volume ratio for efficient transport.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>👁️ Optics</h3>
                <p>Circular lenses focus light through refraction. Microscopes, telescopes, and cameras all depend on circular optical elements.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>⚛️ Atomic Models</h3>
                <p>Early atomic models depicted electrons in circular orbits. Modern quantum mechanics still uses circular symmetry in angular momentum.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Arts & Design</h2>
        <div class="info-grid">
            <div class="info-card">
